# Legacy WordPress URLs -> current SPA routes.
#
# The old insurefirst.ae was WordPress with an /insurance-consultancy/<category>/<product>/
# tree and dated /YYYY/MM/DD/ blog posts. Those URLs are still indexed and still taking
# traffic (GA4 property 365262845 recorded ~60 distinct legacy paths in the last 12 months).
#
# Without these rules the SPA fallback in wrangler.jsonc serves index.html with HTTP 200
# for every one of them, React Router falls through to NotFoundPage, and a visitor who
# wanted a specific product gets a generic 404 instead of the page that replaced it.
#
# TWO THINGS MATTER HERE, both verified against `wrangler dev`:
#
#  1. Trailing slashes are NOT normalized. `/contact-us` and `/contact-us/` are distinct
#     rules, and WordPress emitted the trailing-slash form, so every literal rule below
#     is written twice. Drop the `/` variant and the real traffic silently falls through
#     to the splat rules at the bottom and lands on a category hub instead of the product.
#
#  2. First match wins, and every literal is kept above every splat. Wrangler also warns
#     when a literal sits below a splat, because that costs a slower lookup.
#
# Generated pairs are kept in path order; edit both lines of a pair together.

